<%# The Organize-mode hub — the "useful with zero AI" argument, and the one
    most visitors won't expect. It leads with the model switched off on
    purpose (docs/ABOUT_PLAN.md §2). %>

<section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-5">
  <p>
    Start here, because this is the part that works with the model turned
    off entirely.
  </p>
  <p>
    Underneath everything else, this app is a place to put the things that
    make up a life: what's happening and when, what you have to do, the
    documents that prove things, the people you care about, and what you
    know. Once those are in one place that belongs to you, a great deal
    stops going wrong — and that happens before any model has read a word.
  </p>
</section>

<%= about_screenshot("calendar") %>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">One calendar, for all of it</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Not a work calendar") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        The cardiology appointment, the car insurance renewal, the school
        holiday and the visa deadline are the same kind of thing — a date
        that will hurt if you miss it — and they belong on the same page.
        Most people's lives are split across a work calendar, a paper letter
        on the fridge and a memory. This is the page where they meet.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Things belong to more than one place") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Your mother's cardiology appointment is a health thing and a family
        thing at once. Rather than making you file it as one and lose it
        under the other, everything here can carry as many labels as it
        honestly has, and turns up under all of them.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">What else lives here</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Today") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        One short list: what's due, what's coming, what's overdue. The page
        to open when you don't know where to start.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Tasks and goals") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        A board of day-sized things. Bigger ambitions go in as one sentence
        and come back broken into steps you can start on — the one place
        here where a model earns its keep immediately.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Notes") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        What you know and what you've been told, kept where the rest of your
        life can reach it.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "The dashboard") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        A read of the week across everything you've switched on: what needs
        attention, and why it thinks so.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Chat") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        For when a form is the wrong shape. It has already read the relevant
        part of your own files, so you can start in the middle.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Reminders") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Any task can ping you on the device you're actually holding: once, at
        the time you pick, or every Thursday night if that's what the trash
        needs, putting itself back on today's list each time.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">Why this comes first</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    An assistant that knows nothing about you can only give you advice you
    could have searched for. Everything genuinely useful the rest of this app
    does — reading your lease before drafting the letter, noticing that a
    renewal lands the week the tuition is due — depends on this layer
    existing. It is also the layer you keep if you ever swap the model out,
    which is the point: the model is a part you can replace, and this is not.
  </p>
</section>
